-- An attribute's value (language.md §11.5, frontend.md §9.7): a constant
-- the compiler knows — a quoted value, a bare name, or a hole holding only
-- a number (negated or not), a string or `True`/`False` — which keeps its
-- instruction when written in a hole; otherwise the instruction alone. A
-- list of pairs written in place, each named by a string literal, also
-- records its entries; a list held in a name, or one whose names are not
-- literals, does not.
view model classes name =
    <div
        id="main"
        hidden
        tabindex={0}
        offset={-1}
        lang={"en"}
        open={True}
        spellcheck={False}
        class={[ ( "row", True ), ( "danger", model.on ), ( "big", False ) ]}
        style={[ ( "color", "red" ), ( "--gap", model.gap ) ]}
    >
        <p class={classes} />
        <p class={[ ( name, True ) ]} />
    </div>
